## 9. Challenges and Lessons Learned

One of the main challenges was preparing the Windows Server virtual machine for Active Directory deployment. Installation issues required troubleshooting before I could proceed.

I also gained a clearer understanding of how Active Directory, DNS, security groups, file permissions, and Group Policy work together.

A major lesson was the difference between creating user accounts and building a manageable access-control structure.

Security groups make permission management more scalable, while Group Policy allows administrators to configure security requirements centrally.

The project also reinforced the importance of validating security configurations rather than assuming a setting is effective simply because it has been configured.

